# Example config file for building in a VM. Customize this to your needs.
# Note that you will have to set up the VM manually. Including:
# - Install MacOS
# - Install Xcode, accept licence agreement
# - Create a case sensitive volume for building
# - Optionally create non-privileged user for builds
# - Enable remote log-in (ssh)
# - Optionally ssh-copy-id (from host to VM)
# - Optionally disable password-based ssh-login in VM
#
# Note: The build VM does not necessarily need to live on the host machine.
#
# This file may include commands needed to ensure the VM is up and running,
# but it's also ok to do so manually.

# The script must set the following variables:
user=builder
host=192.168.64.2
vmsrcdir=/Users/${user}/gpg4winvm/src       # where to keep sources
vmbuilddir=/Volumes/BuildFS                 # where to build

# The script may optionally set the following variables:
codesign_id="Apple Development"             # Alternatively, set to "-" for local signing. Default (empty) means no signing
codesign_teamid=                            # For selection of the correct provisioning profile
sync="no"                                   # If the source dir is already mapped to vmsrcdir in your VM
                                            # you can shave a few seconds of the build time by setting this.
